  "global_gates": [
    "Phase 2 requires an approved measurable business goal and owner before Phase 3.",
    "Phase 5 requires explicit approval of the product solution, its rejected alternatives, and the reconciliation of competitive research and prototypes against the PRD.",
    "Phase 6 engineering requirements require user approval before Phase 7.",
    "Phase 7 module map requires user approval before Phase 8, and every open question in erd.md carries a named owner.",
    "Phase 8 must resolve implementation-critical reuse choices and freeze the API verification contract before Phase 9.",
    "Phases 6, 7 and 8 each record a right-sizing judgement naming the problem's complexity, the solution size it warrants, and what was deliberately not built.",
    "Phase 11 is mandatory for code changes unless explicitly waived.",
    "Phase 16 cannot be skipped and validates the append-only harness execution trace.",
    "AI-bearing work requires versioned model, prompt, context, retrieval, tool, and safety contracts with evaluation thresholds before implementation.",
    "Phase 18 cannot be skipped when a pull request is in scope.",
    "Phase 20 production writes require explicit user authorization.",
    "Architecture chain visibility: at Phases 6, 7 and 8, state whether a certified architecture handoff is in force and which decisions it binds."
  ]
}
